#: rc.cpp:269
msgid "Replace with:"
msgstr "Remprazar con:"

#: rc.cpp:270
msgid "Replace all spaces"
msgstr "Remprazar tódolos espacios"

#: rc.cpp:271
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will replace all spaces in all filenames "
"with the specified characters.\n"
"<p>For example with an underscore: 'my good file.ext' becomes "
"'my_good_file.ext'"
msgstr ""
"<p>Se se activa esta opción, K3b remprazará tódolos espacios en tódolos "
"nomes de ficheiros cos caracteres especificados.\n"
"<p>Por exemplo, cun guión subíndice: 'o meu ficheiro.ext' troca por "
"'o_meu_ficheiro.ext'"

#: rc.cpp:273
msgid "The string to replace spaces with"
msgstr "A cadea para rempraza-los espacios"

#: rc.cpp:274
msgid "Extended strip"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:275
msgid "Remove all spaces and capitalize the letters following them"
msgstr "Borrar tódolos espacios e facer maiúsculas as letras que os seguen"

#: rc.cpp:276
msgid ""
"<p>"
"If this option is checked K3b will remove all spaces in all filenames and "
"capitalize all letters following a space.\n"
"<p>Example: 'my good file.ext' becomes 'myGoodFile.ext'"
msgstr ""
"<p>Se se activa esta opción, K3b borrará tódolos espacios en tódolos "
"nomes dos ficheiros e faranse maiúsculas as letras seguidas dun espacio.\n"
"<p>Exemplo: 'o meu ficheiro.ext' troca por 'oMeuFicheiro.ext'"

#: rc.cpp:277
msgid "File Systems"
msgstr "Sistemas de Ficheiros"

#: rc.cpp:278
msgid "Generate Rock Ridge extensions"
msgstr "Xerar extensións Rock Ridge"

#: rc.cpp:279
msgid "Add Rock Ridge extensions to the CD"
msgstr "Engadir extensións Rock Ridge ó CD"

#: rc.cpp:280
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will generate the System Use Sharing "
"Protocol records (SUSP) specified by the Rock Ridge Interchange Protocol "
"(IEEE-P1282).\n"
"<p>Rock Ridge extends the ISO-9660 filesystem by features equal to the UNIX "
"filesystems (permissions, symbolic links, very long filenames, ...). It uses "
"ISO-8859 or UTF-16 based characters and allows 255 octets.\n"
"<p>Rock Ridge extensions are located at the end of each ISO-9660 directory "
"record. This makes the Rock Ridge tree closely coupled to the ISO-9660 "
"tree.\n"
"<p><b>It is highly recommended to use Rock Ridge extensions on every data "
"CD.</b>"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:281
msgid "Generate Joliet extensions"
msgstr "Xerar extensións Joliet"

#: rc.cpp:282
msgid "Add Joliet extensions to the CD"
msgstr "Engadir extensións Joliet ó CD"

#: rc.cpp:283
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will add additional Joliet extensions to "
"the CD.\n"
"<p>Joliet is not an accepted independent international standard like "
"ISO-9660 or Rock Ridge. It is mainly used on Windows systems.\n"
"<p>Joliet does not allow all characters, so the Joliet filenames are not "
"identical to the filenames on disk (as compared to Rock Ridge). Joliet has a "
"filename length limitation of 64 chars (independent from the character "
"coding and type e.g. European vs. Japanese). This is annoying, as modern "
"file systems all allow 255 characters per path name component.\n"
"<p>Joliet uses UTF-16 coding.\n"
"<p><b>Caution:</b> With the exception of Linux and FreeBSD, there is no "
"POSIX-like OS that supports Joliet. So <b>never create Joliet only CDs</b> "
"for that reason."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:284
msgid "Generate Udf structures"
msgstr "Xerar estructuras Udf"

#: rc.cpp:285
msgid "Add Udf structures to the CD"
msgstr "Engadir estructuras Udf ó CD"

#: rc.cpp:286
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked K3b will create Udf filesystem structures in "
"addition to the Iso9660 filesystem.\n"
"<p>The Udf (<em><b>U</b>niversal <b>D</b>isk <b>F</b>ormat</em>) is mainly "
"used for DVDs."
msgstr ""
"<p>"
"Se se activa esta opción K3b creará estructuras do sistema de ficheiros "
"Udf ademáis de ó sistema de ficheiros Iso9660.\n"
"<p>O Udf (<em><b>U</b>niversal <b>D</b>isk <b>F</b>ormat</em>) emprégase "
"principalmente para DVDs."

#: rc.cpp:287
msgid "Symbolic Links"
msgstr "Ligazóns Simbólicas"

#: rc.cpp:288
msgid "Discard all symlinks"
msgstr "Descartar tódalas ligazóns simbólicas"

#: rc.cpp:289
msgid "Do not create symbolic links on CD"
msgstr "Non crear ligazóns simbólicas no CD"

#: rc.cpp:290
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will ignore all symbolic links that have "
"been added to the project; meaning that the resulting CD will have no links "
"at all.\n"
"<p><b>Caution:</b> Symbolic links require Rock Ridge extensions!"
msgstr ""
"<p>Se se activa esta opción, K3b ignorará tódalas ligazóns simbólicas "
"que se engadan ó proxecto, significando que o CD resultante non terá "
"ligazóns.\n"
"<p><b>Precaución:</b> As ligazóns simbólicas requiren extensións Rock "
"Ridge!"

#: rc.cpp:291
msgid "Discard broken symlinks"
msgstr "Descartar ligazóns simbólicas rotas"

#: rc.cpp:292
msgid "Ignore all links pointing outside the project"
msgstr "Ignorar tódalas ligazóns simbólicas que apunten a fóra do proxecto"

#: rc.cpp:293
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, K3b will discard all symbolic links that do "
"not point to a file inside the project. That includes all links to absolute "
"paths like '/home/myhome/testfile'.\n"
"<p><b>Caution:</b> Symbolic links require Rock Ridge extensions!"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:295
msgid "Preserve file permissions (backup)"
msgstr "Preserva-los permisos dos ficheiros (copia de seguridade)"

#: rc.cpp:296
msgid ""
"<p>If this option is checked, all files on the resulting CD will have "
"exactly the same permissions as the source files. (Otherwise all files will "
"have equal permissions and be owned by root).\n"
"<p>This is mainly useful for backups.\n"
"<p><b>Caution:</b> The permissions may not make much sense on other file "
"systems. For example if a user that owns a file on the CD does not exist."
msgstr ""

